\f0\fs24 \cf2 The capitals in the library are not there by chance: they are the result of a meticulous search conducted by the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers, who had an obsession with details. One in particular stands out immediately: the skull. Yes, you read that right. A small skull drawn in black ink on graph paper, a symbol of memento mori.\
During the Renaissance, this type of symbol was widely used: a way to remind people that life is short, and that everything can end in an instant. A grim thought? Perhaps. But also an invitation to live with awareness.\
And this is not the only skull in the house. Some are hidden right here in the library. Others are scattered throughout the museum. Will you be able to find them all? Detail by detail, the home of the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers always reveals something more.\
